## 4. Scope Governance Boundaries

Explicitly documenting exclusions protects sprint velocity and prevents informal feature creep during execution.

### `[IN-SCOPE]` — Committed Deliverables
- [ ] Core discovery, technical site/architecture audit, and pre-mortem risk register
- [ ] Vendor TCO evaluation, procurement, and SLA contracting
- [ ] System integration, phased pilot launch (`[N]` locations / user cohorts), and QA validation
- [ ] Role-based staff onboarding, Train-the-Trainer certification, and SOP handover

### `[OUT-OF-SCOPE]` — Explicitly Excluded from Current Phase
- [ ] Full-scale rollout prior to passing Pilot Go/No-Go quality gates
- [ ] Legacy policy overhauls (e.g., comp/refund rules, HR payroll restructuring)
- [ ] Custom feature requests not tied to the core KPIs listed in Section 3 *(routed to Phase 2 backlog)*

---

## 5. Phased Delivery Roadmap & Quality Gates

| Phase | Duration | Primary Deliverable | Mandatory Quality Gate |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **1. Initiation & Scope** | `2 Weeks` | Signed Charter, Stakeholder Matrix, Risk Register | **Gate 1:** Scope & Compliance Sign-Off |
| **2. Sourcing & Infra Readiness** | `4 Weeks` | Vendor selection, network/infra audit, staging QA | **Gate 2:** Infrastructure & Buffer Clearance |
| **3. Integration & Pilot Launch** | `4 Weeks` | Live integration, phased pilot, rapid friction fixes | **Gate 3:** Pilot KPI & Stability Validation |
| **4. Retrospective & Scale** | `2 Weeks` | Impact report, SOP lock, rollout decision | **Gate 4:** Executive Scale Readiness |

---

## 6. Stakeholder Governance & Decision Rights

| Quadrant (Power / Interest) | Role / Group | Engagement Cadence | Primary Governance Focus |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Manage Closely** *(High / High)* | Executive Sponsor, Ops Director | Bi-weekly Steering | Budget, scope trade-offs, escalation clearance |
| **Keep Satisfied** *(High / Low)* | Legal / Compliance, Department Heads | Milestone Reviews | Regulatory gates, operational continuity |
| **Keep Informed** *(Low / High)* | Frontline & Delivery Teams | Daily Stand-ups / Weekly Syncs | Workflow friction, training, adoption feedback |
| **Monitor** *(Low / Low)* | External Vendors / Consultants | Ad-hoc / SLA Checkpoints | Lead times, warranty & uptime SLAs |

